course: dictionary
lesson: 1926
title: Comforting words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Comforting means making you feel calmer, safer, or less sad or worried. Comforting words, a comforting hug, and a comforting smell all do this job. Look at the words around the word for clues. «The nurse spoke in a soft, comforting voice, and Sam stopped crying.» The voice helped Sam feel better, so comforting means something that helps you feel calmer.
explain: Comfort is also a verb: it means helping someone who is upset to feel better. «Ella sat next to her friend and comforted her after the match.» Comforting is the -ing form of that verb, so you will also see phrases like «comforting a friend».
explain: Look at how the word fits the sentence. «A comforting truth, like "It was not your fault", is the best kind of kindness.» The words make you feel better, and they are kind and true. Ask yourself: would this sentence still make sense if I put "calming" or "helpful" in its place?
explain: Comforting does not always mean true or safe. «A comforting saying is not a safety rule; for lightning, follow official advice such as the Met Office's.» A kind saying can make you feel better, but in real danger you need facts from a trusted source.
fact: Comforting means making you feel calmer, safer, or less sad or worried.
fact: Comfort is also a verb: «comforting a friend» means helping someone who is upset to feel better.
fact: Good ways to comfort a sad friend include listening, saying a kind word, sitting with them, and getting an adult to help.
fact: «Comfort food» is food that makes you feel cosy and happy.
fact: A comforting saying can make you feel better, but it is not a safety rule. For lightning, follow official advice.
exercise: «The teacher's comforting words helped Ali stop feeling scared.» What does comforting mean here? | Something to eat | Making him feel more worried | Loud and fast | *Making him feel calmer and safer
exercise: Maya's friend is upset, so Maya sits with her and says a kind word. What is Maya doing? | Forgetting her friend | *Comforting her friend | Scaring her friend | Shouting at her friend
exercise: Which word could replace comforting in «a comforting smell of bread baking»? | Loud | Confusing | Frightening | *Warm and cosy
test: «The ducklings huddled together, comforted by their mother's warm feathers.» What does comforted mean here? | Made to run away | Made to sleep outside | Made to feel angrier | *Made to feel safer
test: Which sentence uses comforting as the -ing form of the verb comfort? | The comforting blanket is soft | *Sam is comforting his little brother after the fall | The comforting sweets are on the shelf
exam: Asha says a comforting saying is always a safety rule. Is she right? | Yes, always | Yes, but only at school | No, because it is always false | *No, a comforting saying can help you feel better but is not a safety rule, so follow official advice in danger
